// %Previous short conversations
//
// Demonstrates that unmatched replies (ERR: No Reply Matched) do not
// overwrite history.reply[0], so %previous context survives
// (aichaos/rivescript-js#411).
//
// Try:
//   explain previous
//   ask me a question
//   lol          → ERR: No Reply Matched  (context kept)
//   2            → Yes!

+ explain previous
- %previous matches the bot's last reply.
^ After I ask a question, number answers use that context.
^ Unmatched input returns ERR: No Reply Matched but keeps
^ the question in history so you can still answer.
^ Say: ask me a question

+ ask me a question
- How many arms do I have?

// Prefer these while the last bot reply was the question
+ [*] # [*]
% how many arms do i have
* <star> == 2 => Yes!
- No!

+ *
% how many arms do i have
- That isn't a number.

// No catch-all on purpose: unmatched turns return ERR: No Reply Matched
// without clearing %previous. Add `+ *` / `- I don't know.` if you want
// to hide the error string from users.
